      "side": 1,
      "message": "shouldBreakDeclOnCommand (line 2284) and startsNewTopLevelCommandInDeclBody (line 2310) recognize imports at any leading offset via parseImportLine(line, leadingPos), but top-level import parsing here gates on colOffset \u003d\u003d 0 and hardcodes startPos \u003d 0. As a result, same-line imports after a block comment, back-to-back imports on one line (\"import A import B theorem bad : False :\u003d sorry\"), or indented imports fall through to a fallback code directive and swallow trailing declarations instead of splitting them out. Parsing from startCol even when colOffset \u003e 0 (and slicing from colOffset on the first line) keeps top-level splitting consistent with declaration boundary detection.",
